<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John J. Pershing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1860">1860</a>–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as John Joseph Pershing, Black Jack Pershing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John J. Pershing was an American army officer who served as military governor of the Moro Province in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1909 to 1913, where he disarmed the population and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bud-bagsak">Battle of Bud Bagsak</a>. He later led the Punitive Expedition into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1916 and commanded the American Expeditionary Forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, becoming General of the Armies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-j-pershing.jpg" alt="John J. Pershing" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain News Service, publisher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_John_Joseph_Pershing_head_on_shoulders.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
